---
title: "Dynamics"
code: "EGR-245"
category: "engineering"
credits: "3"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/EGR-240"
corequisites: []
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisites: EGR 240 or departmental approval"
---

Presents approach to kinematics of particles in linear and curvilinear motion. Includes kinematics of rigid bodies in plane motion. Teaches Newton's second law, work-energy and power, impulse and momentum, and problem-solving using computers. Lecture 3 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
